\[\sin^5 x - \cos^5 x = \frac{\sin x - \cos x}{\sin x \cos x}.\]Note that
\[\sin x - \cos x \le \sqrt{2} \le 2,\]so
\[\sin^5 x - \cos^5 x \le \sin x \cos x.\]Now,
\begin{align*}
\sin^5 x - \sin x \cos^2 x &= \sin x (\sin^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\
&= \sin x ((1 - \cos^2 x)^2 - \cos^2 x) \\
&= \sin x (\cos^4 x - 2 \cos^2 x + 1).
\end{align*}Since $\cos^2 x \le 1,$ $\sin^5 x \le \sin x.$  Therefore,
\begin{align*}
\sin^5 x - \sin x \cos^2 x &\le \sin x (0 - 1) \\
&= -\sin x \\
&\le -0.5.
\end{align*}Also,
\begin{align*}
\sin^5 x - \sin x &\ge \sin x ((-1)^5 - (-1)) = 0,\\
\sin^5 x - \cos^5 x &\ge 1^{1/3} - (-1)^{1/3} = 2, \\
\sin x \cos^2 x &\le 1,
\end{align*}so
\[\sin x \le \frac{1}{2}.\]Therefore, all solutions $x$ lie in the interval $[0^\circ, 360^\circ],$ and $x$ cannot be in any of the intervals $\boxed{\left[ 0^\circ, 15^{\circ} \right), \left[ 345 \|^\circ,\, 90^\circ \right]},$ as can be verified from the equation graphically. Note that $x \approx 19.47^\circ$ is the solution to $\sin x = 0.0312097.$

